    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0219" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg139"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Swenson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 113.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 197, of the 26th ultimo, relative
                    to the detention of Sören L. Sörensen, a naturalized citizen of the United
                    States, for military duty, has been received.</p>
                <p>The note of the minister of foreign affairs to yourself of March 12 ultimo would
                    seem to throw upon Mr. Sörensen the onus of showing that his acts, as recited in
                    the note, do not evince an intention on his part to acquire a permanent domicile
                    in Jutland, and your letter of the 16th ultimo in that sense to Mr. Sörensen
                    has, therefore, the Department’s approval.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
